### HIR import registration resolution facts

#### resolves a qualified type name once per (surface, name), not once per importer

- Verify: resolves a qualified type name once per (surface, name), not once per importer
   - Expected: lowering.explicit_dep_scan_count equals `1`
   - Expected: lowering.explicit_dep_scan_count equals `1`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 21 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: resolves a qualified type name once per (surface, name), not once per importer")
val registry = import_registry()
var lowering = hirlowering_for_module("pkg/imp1.spl", registry)
val span = Span.empty()
val decl = registry.surfaces[0]
# Three importers of the SAME declaring surface, asking for the SAME
# signature dependency. One lowerer serves the whole phase
# (stage3_hir_lowerer_reuse_contract_spec.spl pins that), so the second
# and third importers must cost a dict probe.
lowering.begin_module("pkg/imp1.spl")
lowering.materialize_imported_callable_explicit_dependency(
    decl, "Widget", span, false)
expect(lowering.explicit_dep_scan_count).to_equal(1)
lowering.begin_module("pkg/imp2.spl")
lowering.materialize_imported_callable_explicit_dependency(
    decl, "Widget", span, false)
lowering.begin_module("pkg/imp3.spl")
lowering.materialize_imported_callable_explicit_dependency(
    decl, "Widget", span, false)
expect(lowering.explicit_dep_scan_count).to_equal(1)
```

</details>

#### does not repeat a MISS -- the negative result is cached too

- Verify: does not repeat a MISS -- the negative result is cached too
   - Expected: lowering.explicit_dep_scan_count equals `1`
   - Expected: lowering.explicit_dep_target_memo["pkg.decl NeverDeclared"] equals `-1`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 13 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: does not repeat a MISS -- the negative result is cached too")
val registry = import_registry()
var lowering = hirlowering_for_module("pkg/imp1.spl", registry)
val span = Span.empty()
val decl = registry.surfaces[0]
# `pkg.decl` has no imports at all, so every query is a miss. A miss is
# exactly the case that used to re-sweep for every importer.
lowering.materialize_imported_callable_explicit_dependency(
    decl, "NeverDeclared", span, false)
lowering.materialize_imported_callable_explicit_dependency(
    decl, "NeverDeclared", span, false)
expect(lowering.explicit_dep_scan_count).to_equal(1)
expect(lowering.explicit_dep_target_memo["pkg.decl NeverDeclared"]).to_equal(-1)
```

</details>

